# Milestone: M3
# Covers: 100k allocate-and-drop cycles complete within a bounded heap;
#         the GC reclaims dead cells and gc_live_bytes remains small relative
#         to gc_total_allocated.
# matrix-row: object-model
#
# `{}` is a block here, not an object literal, so the loop allocates with
# `Object.new()`.  What a fixture can see is the loop completing all
# 100000 rounds without an out-of-memory error; the bounded-heap half --
# the peak staying small while the total allocated grows -- is pinned in
# C, under a counting allocator, by
# tests/rt/test_obj.c::an_object_loop_runs_in_bounded_memory.
var alloc_drop = function() { var i = 0; while (i < 100000) { var x = Object.new(); x = nil; i = i + 1 }; i }
alloc_drop()
[00000001] <?>
[00000002] 100000
